abstract: >-
  ENTITY is an open protocol and reference implementation for persistent digital
  identity, delegated authority, provenance and evidence, rights, portable
  recovery, and interoperable economic state. ENTITY v3.4.3 is a bounded
  remediation release based on immutable v3.4.2 evidence. The Blackmore
  Technology Data Universe (BTDU) component remains version 3.4.2 unchanged in
  ENTITY v3.4.3 and provides an ENTITY-governed atom/bond information substrate
  connected to authority, rights, provenance, recovery, and economic boundaries.
keywords:
  - sovereign digital authority
  - digital identity
  - delegated authorization
  - data provenance
  - data governance
  - data rights
  - protocol conformance
  - clean-room interoperability
  - portable recovery
  - open protocol
  - BTDU
